@startuml architecture
title Phylogenetic Visualization Library - Simplified Architecture
left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

package "Server App" {
  class api {
    +ingestDataset()
    +getCanonicalDataset()
    +getLodBundle()
  }

  class core {
    +validateInvariants()
    +buildCanonicalContracts()
  }

  class data {
    +parseNewick()
    +parseEdgeList()
    +normalizeCanonicalDataset()
    +buildMetadataIndex()
  }

  class clustering {
    +buildLodBundle()
    +buildThresholdClusters()
    +buildDepthClusters()
  }

  class CanonicalDataset
  class LodBundle
}

package "Client App" {
  class input {
    +uploadNewick()
    +selectDataset()
    +setInitialConfig()
  }

  class layout {
    +computeForceLayout()
    +computePositions()
  }

  class render {
    +toGraphology()
    +applyNodePrograms()
    +applyReducers()
  }

  class state {
    +handleZoomTransitions()
    +applyFilters()
    +handleSelection()
  }

  class PositionedGraph
}

input --> api : dataset/config request
api --> data : ingest request
core ..> CanonicalDataset : validates
data --> CanonicalDataset : outputs
api --> CanonicalDataset : response payload
CanonicalDataset --> layout : input
layout --> PositionedGraph : outputs
PositionedGraph --> render : render input
state --> layout : recompute request
state --> render : interaction events
render --> state : selection/camera feedback

clustering ..> CanonicalDataset : consumes
clustering --> LodBundle : outputs
LodBundle ..> state : semantic zoom levels
api --> LodBundle : clustering response (phase 2)

note bottom of render
Renderer adapter only.
No phylogenetic semantics here.
end note

note right of clustering
Phase 2 module:
implemented after
core+data integration is stable.
end note

@enduml